-- The trait's module writes the impl for a type of a third module, and
-- for `Int`. Whoever calls a method of the trait imports the trait's
-- module, so its `let`s are set before the first call, in the `let`s
-- of another module too.
import early

fn main() {
  println(early.first)
  println(early.second)
  println(early.third)
}
